{"id":"000W2D","title":"Kroopki Chaos (9x9)","author":"Oddlyeven","solvedCount":0,"difficulty":4,"rating":"N/A","firstSeen":"2026-11-16T02:48:48+00:00","posted":"Heute, 03:26 Uhr","rules":"This puzzle is part of the puzzle pack Chaotic Construction by the Sudoku Skunkworks. Please check it out!\n\nFor an introductory 6x6 puzzle using these rules, please check out Kroopki Chaos (6x6).\nRules:\n\nChaos Construction: Divide the grid into regions of 9 orthogonally connected cells each, such that every cell is part of exactly one region. Place the digits 1 to 9 exactly once in each row, column and region.\n\nKroopki doots: Doots are thick lines between sets of cells. A white doot separates two sets of cells whose respective sums are consecutive. A black doot separates two sets of cells whose respective sums are in a 1:2 ratio. Doots also act as region borders.\n\nSight circles: Digits in circles indicate the number of cells seen horizontally and vertically within the same region, including itself. Cells from other regions block vision.\n\nExample grid (not intended to be solvable):\n\nSudokuPad - Penpa+","solutionCode":"Row 7, left to right, with a - for each internal region border.","tags":["Sudoku","Chaos Construction (Variante)"],"links":[{"url":"https://sudokupad.app/p4ywl621tw","kind":"sudokupad"},{"url":"https://tinyurl.com/5n893zzf","kind":"short"}],"data":"","error":null,"settings":{},"link":"https://sudokupad.app/p4ywl621tw","linkKind":"sudokupad","summary":{"format":"scl","decoded":true,"rows":9,"cols":9,"cages":0,"hasSolution":true,"features":["lines","overlays"]},"attempts":0,"fetched":"2026-11-16T02:48:48+00:00"}